WEBVTT

1
00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.933
<i>In Reykjavik, Iceland today,</i>

2
00:01:40.935 --> 00:01:44.903
<i>Bobby Fischer failed to show up for his
second game against Boris Spassky.</i>

3
00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:59.885
<i>Unpredictable Bobby Fischer
stayed in bed today</i>

4
00:01:59.887 --> 00:02:01.787
<i>rather than show up for game 2</i>

5
00:02:01.789 --> 00:02:05.290
<i>in his world title match with chess
champion Boris Spassky of Russia.</i>

6
00:02:05.292 --> 00:02:08.794
<i>The match between the world's chess
champion, Boris Spassky, and Bobby Fischer</i>

7
00:02:08.796 --> 00:02:10.762
<i>took a strange turn</i>

8
00:02:10.764 --> 00:02:15.567
<i>when Fischer failed to show up at the
scheduled time and forfeited game 2.</i>

9
00:02:15.569 --> 00:02:18.770
<i>The entire world seems
to be asking the same question:</i>

10
00:02:18.772 --> 00:02:20.839
<i>"What will Bobby Fischer
do next?"</i>

11
00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:46.444
Half the witnesses they
call are communists.

12
00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:47.659
The other half are Jews.

13
00:03:47.661 --> 00:03:49.528
If you're both,
do you testify twice?

14
00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:51.196
- Go ahead.
- Make jokes, Mr. liberal.

15
00:03:51.198 --> 00:03:53.599
Your entire family wasn't
gassed at the camps.

16
00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:04.543
Mama.

17
00:04:04.545 --> 00:04:06.345
Mama! Not now, Bobby.

18
00:04:06.347 --> 00:04:08.847
I have to talk to you!

19
00:04:11.051 --> 00:04:12.784
Bobby, it's past your bedtime.

20
00:04:12.786 --> 00:04:14.553
Joan?

21
00:04:14.555 --> 00:04:17.022
There's a car out there!

22
00:04:17.024 --> 00:04:19.524
- What car?
- You told me to tell you.

23
00:04:19.526 --> 00:04:21.460
A red 1952 Chevy.

24
00:04:26.867 --> 00:04:30.202
Bobby, you remember
what I told you?

25
00:04:30.204 --> 00:04:33.572
There are bad people out there
who wanna intimidate us

26
00:04:33.574 --> 00:04:37.609
because we represent something very
threatening to them, to the status quo.

27
00:04:37.611 --> 00:04:39.911
You remember what that is?
Revolution.

28
00:04:39.913 --> 00:04:44.216
Yes. And sometimes these bad
people wanna know about our work.

29
00:04:44.218 --> 00:04:46.051
So they spy on us.

30
00:04:46.053 --> 00:04:48.987
So... if someone comes up
to you in the street

31
00:04:48.989 --> 00:04:51.957
and asks you questions about me or
mommy's friends, what do you say?

32
00:04:51.959 --> 00:04:53.392
"I have nothing to say to you."

33
00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:56.795
That's my big boy.

34
00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:02.434
Yuck. Joan. Joan. Joan. He's
got mustard on his shirt.

35
00:05:02.436 --> 00:05:03.969
He's gotta wear that
to school tomorrow.

36
00:05:03.971 --> 00:05:06.738
- Would you soak it for me?
- Love to.

37
00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:09.408
- And put him to bed.
<i>- Bedtime for Bonzo.</i>

38
00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:49.074
I'm Carmine Nigro, and I'm
told you are a chess player.

39
00:06:49.076 --> 00:06:52.511
Our church... all colors
and creeds welcome.

40
00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.787
Bobby.

41
00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:05.123
Choose.

42
00:07:06.893 --> 00:07:09.528
Let's see what we got here, eh?

43
00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:13.198
Most young people don't have the
concentration to play at a high level,

44
00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.133
so please don't get
your hopes up.

45
00:07:15.135 --> 00:07:18.703
Ha! He's beaten everyone
he's ever played.

46
00:07:18.705 --> 00:07:21.873
My hopes are he will give up on the
damn game if someone beats him.

47
00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:25.377
Okay. It's your move.

48
00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:29.881
Do you like baseball, Bobby?

49
00:07:29.883 --> 00:07:34.252
- Hmm? Jackie Robinson? Pee wee Reese?
- Mm-hmm.

50
00:07:34.254 --> 00:07:36.555
Bobby, have you ever been
to the moon on the subway?

51
00:07:36.557 --> 00:07:38.490
Mmhmm.

52
00:07:38.492 --> 00:07:42.160
If I take the pieces away, he just keeps
playing in his head. Day and night.

53
00:07:42.162 --> 00:07:44.496
Took him to a shrink.
He said to come here.

54
00:07:44.498 --> 00:07:48.366
Well, his game is good.
Not exceptional though.

55
00:07:52.805 --> 00:07:54.339
Hmm.

56
00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:08.687
- Who taught him to move like this?
- He taught himself.

57
00:08:13.526 --> 00:08:16.361
Bobby, shall we call it a draw?

58
00:08:18.364 --> 00:08:20.398
Hmm?

59
00:08:26.005 --> 00:08:28.773
He hates draws.

60
00:08:39.452 --> 00:08:41.286
Check.

61
00:08:48.628 --> 00:08:50.061
Mate.

62
00:09:08.648 --> 00:09:11.316
I'm officially the 25th best
chess player in New York City.

63
00:09:11.318 --> 00:09:13.218
I can tell you
he has great potential.

64
00:09:23.696 --> 00:09:25.463
Come here. Come...

65
00:09:29.335 --> 00:09:31.069
again.

66
00:09:31.071 --> 00:09:33.271
Carmine, it's your move!

67
00:09:33.273 --> 00:09:35.040
I know it's my move.

68
00:09:35.042 --> 00:09:37.475
Come on! I'm thinking.

69
00:09:42.883 --> 00:09:44.950
<i>Come on, carmine.
It's your turn.</i>

70
00:09:44.952 --> 00:09:47.619
Bobby, I know it's my turn.
Just go.

71
00:09:52.559 --> 00:09:55.627
- <i>Come on!
- Bobby, I still have time on the clock, okay?</i>

72
00:09:55.629 --> 00:09:57.429
- <i>Let me think.</i>
- Fine.

73
00:10:10.611 --> 00:10:12.777
<i>There's a rising star
in the chess world,</i>

74
00:10:12.779 --> 00:10:14.546
<i>and he's only 12 years old.</i>

75
00:10:14.548 --> 00:10:16.481
<i>His name is Bobby Fischer.</i>

76
00:10:16.483 --> 00:10:19.084
<i>Today he played
American master Donald Byrne</i>

77
00:10:19.086 --> 00:10:23.154
and beat him in what is already being
described as the game of the century.

78
00:10:23.156 --> 00:10:24.823
So, Bobby, what's next for you?

79
00:10:24.825 --> 00:10:28.126
It's either I beat them,
or they beat me. You know?

80
00:10:28.128 --> 00:10:30.428
<i>With an impressive string
of five victories,</i>

81
00:10:30.430 --> 00:10:33.732
<i>Bobby today became the youngest
ever United States chess champion.</i>

82
00:11:48.574 --> 00:11:50.241
Ooh.

83
00:12:21.107 --> 00:12:23.274
Oh, you're back.

84
00:12:23.276 --> 00:12:25.744
And you won. Congratulations.

85
00:12:27.747 --> 00:12:29.781
Every night
I hear you two screw.

86
00:12:29.783 --> 00:12:32.584
Bobby, put those down. Bobby.

87
00:12:32.586 --> 00:12:36.287
Shut up, size 12. You live in<i> my
</i> house, and you're not my father.

88
00:12:36.289 --> 00:12:37.756
Okay? Bobby.

89
00:12:37.758 --> 00:12:39.624
- Where<i> is</i> my father?
- Come on.

90
00:12:39.626 --> 00:12:41.760
I was born, right?
What did you do with him?

91
00:12:41.762 --> 00:12:43.762
Is he on earth?
Does he even exist?

92
00:12:43.764 --> 00:12:46.965
Honey, that was
a long time ago.

93
00:12:46.967 --> 00:12:50.101
So what? You can't remember?
Where is he?

94
00:12:50.103 --> 00:12:51.302
Gone.

95
00:12:51.304 --> 00:12:53.538
- Gone where?
- It doesn't matter.

96
00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:55.640
It matters to me.

97
00:12:58.244 --> 00:13:00.111
You know what?

98
00:13:00.113 --> 00:13:01.946
Get the fuck out of here.

99
00:13:01.948 --> 00:13:05.550
You know wha... go... go back to
Moscow with your commie friends.

100
00:13:05.552 --> 00:13:08.787
I am studying day and night.

101
00:13:08.789 --> 00:13:10.622
And I'm gonna be
the next world champion.

102
00:13:10.624 --> 00:13:13.625
Do you understand me?
I need silence.

103
00:13:13.627 --> 00:13:16.594
Do you understand?
I want silence.

104
00:13:29.408 --> 00:13:31.643
Mom says you're staying
at the chess club.

105
00:13:31.645 --> 00:13:33.211
It's quiet there.

106
00:13:36.115 --> 00:13:37.916
And what
about high school? Hmm?

107
00:13:37.918 --> 00:13:39.651
Huh. Yeah.

108
00:13:39.653 --> 00:13:41.519
She still there?

109
00:13:41.521 --> 00:13:43.621
She fixed up the apartment.

110
00:13:43.623 --> 00:13:46.024
Even got the hot-water
heater working.

111
00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:50.662
She won't be
living there anymore.

112
00:13:50.664 --> 00:13:54.299
She's going to do politics
in California with cyril.

113
00:13:54.301 --> 00:13:56.467
You mean king Kong. Mate.

114
00:13:56.469 --> 00:13:58.369
Mom was worried.

115
00:13:58.371 --> 00:14:01.873
She thought if they went
away, you'd go home,

116
00:14:01.875 --> 00:14:04.008
sleep in a bed.

117
00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:05.643
That's what she told you? Huh?

118
00:14:05.645 --> 00:14:07.946
And you bought it?

119
00:14:07.948 --> 00:14:11.015
She's running away with some
nutcase bigfoot communist.

120
00:14:11.017 --> 00:14:13.351
Oh, oh, and you know what?
It's for Bobby's benefit.

121
00:14:13.353 --> 00:14:15.787
You said you wanted quiet.

122
00:14:15.789 --> 00:14:18.122
You won, Bobby.

123
00:14:18.124 --> 00:14:19.757
Be happy.

124
00:14:25.197 --> 00:14:27.365
<i>In Portoroz, Yugoslavia today,</i>

125
00:14:27.367 --> 00:14:29.234
<i>American chess prodigy
Bobby Fischer</i>

126
00:14:29.236 --> 00:14:32.370
<i>became the youngest ever grandmaster
in the history of the game.</i>

127
00:14:32.372 --> 00:14:35.673
Congratulations, Bobby.
Where do you go from here?

128
00:14:35.675 --> 00:14:38.476
Well, uh, I wanna play
the Russians.

129
00:14:38.478 --> 00:14:40.759
They're the best in the world,
and I'm gonna beat 'em all.

130
00:15:04.504 --> 00:15:06.104
<i>Having won the interzonal,</i>

131
00:15:06.106 --> 00:15:08.439
<i>he is the odds-on favorite to
win the candidates tournament</i>

132
00:15:08.441 --> 00:15:11.409
<i>and gain a match against
the current world champion.</i>

133
00:15:16.616 --> 00:15:20.785
How are you feeling? I'm ready.
It's my time.

134
00:15:59.459 --> 00:16:01.793
Mr. Spassky,
a quick chat, please.

135
00:16:53.145 --> 00:16:54.812
This is ridiculous.

136
00:16:54.814 --> 00:16:57.315
King to rook three.
Knight to king six.

137
00:16:57.317 --> 00:17:00.251
Pawn takes queen. Bishop to knight seven.
It's over.

138
00:17:04.857 --> 00:17:08.026
The Russians are drawing games on
purpose to save their strength

139
00:17:08.028 --> 00:17:09.861
and they're dumping games
to pad their points,

140
00:17:09.863 --> 00:17:12.663
making it statistically
impossible for me to win.

141
00:17:12.665 --> 00:17:14.749
Mr. Fischer, your complaint
has been lodged.

142
00:17:14.775 --> 00:17:16.000
There's nothing we can do.

143
00:17:16.002 --> 00:17:17.702
Of course there's
something you can do.

144
00:17:17.704 --> 00:17:20.471
They're playing a team game. It's
five guys against one. Against me!

145
00:17:20.473 --> 00:17:22.540
Can we go back inside?
No, I'm not interested.

146
00:17:22.542 --> 00:17:24.575
Bobby, don't... what the hell are
you doing about this anyways?

147
00:17:24.577 --> 00:17:27.345
All right. Come here. Gather around.
I got something to say.

148
00:17:27.347 --> 00:17:29.680
I wanna make this very clear.

149
00:17:29.682 --> 00:17:31.549
The Russians are cheats.

150
00:17:31.551 --> 00:17:33.484
Everybody knows
what's going on.

151
00:17:33.486 --> 00:17:35.987
The corrupt federation
does nothing to stop it!

152
00:17:35.989 --> 00:17:39.490
There can be no legitimate world
champ if I'm not playing.

153
00:17:39.492 --> 00:17:42.727
And I'm not gonna play,
because this is unfair.

154
00:17:42.729 --> 00:17:45.730
It's unjust. It's immoral!
I quit.

155
00:17:45.732 --> 00:17:48.833
I don't just quit this tournament.
I am quitting chess.

156
00:17:48.835 --> 00:17:52.570
Move. Move.

157
00:17:52.572 --> 00:17:54.072
Bobby.

158
00:17:54.074 --> 00:17:57.408
Bobby, wait. We'll go back
inside and apologize.

159
00:17:57.410 --> 00:17:59.343
You can still place well.
What are you talking about?

160
00:17:59.345 --> 00:18:01.212
This was it!

161
00:18:01.214 --> 00:18:04.382
What do you think I've been working
the past 10 years of my life for?

162
00:18:04.384 --> 00:18:08.419
I was gonna be the youngest world champ in
the history of the game! That's over now!

163
00:18:08.421 --> 00:18:11.189
They stole it from me, carmine.
They took it!

164
00:18:11.191 --> 00:18:14.292
That was today! Today!

165
00:19:24.863 --> 00:19:27.365
- English.
- This is America.

166
00:19:30.102 --> 00:19:33.337
Ah, the American boy who hates us,
but cannot resist our magazines.

167
00:19:33.339 --> 00:19:35.873
Spassky is becoming
the new Messiah.

168
00:19:35.875 --> 00:19:38.743
They say he won't
ever lose a match.

169
00:19:40.012 --> 00:19:42.880
Someone left this for you.

170
00:19:42.882 --> 00:19:44.682
A lawyer.

171
00:19:44.684 --> 00:19:46.617
You are in trouble, maybe?

172
00:20:16.682 --> 00:20:18.616
Do you want a game?

173
00:20:19.551 --> 00:20:21.252
You think I'm stupid?

174
00:20:21.254 --> 00:20:24.021
So you know who I am.
Yeah, I know who you are.

175
00:20:24.023 --> 00:20:26.757
I've been trying to reach you.
You don't answer your phone.

176
00:20:27.893 --> 00:20:30.561
Oh. You're...
you're that lawyer.

177
00:20:30.563 --> 00:20:32.863
What'd I do? Nothing.

178
00:20:32.865 --> 00:20:34.699
Nothing. You did nothing.

179
00:20:34.701 --> 00:20:37.335
You do nothing.
That's why I'm here.

180
00:20:37.337 --> 00:20:39.403
I read your article
in<i> sports illustrated.</i>

181
00:20:39.405 --> 00:20:41.872
You told the truth about the Russians.
Yeah, that's right, I did.

182
00:20:41.874 --> 00:20:43.641
Did you see this?

183
00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:48.546
"Soviet invasion
to hit California surf."

184
00:20:48.548 --> 00:20:51.549
"World's greatest chess players
to visit us." Yeah, I saw that.

185
00:20:51.551 --> 00:20:55.853
They say it's just a game... for fun,
hand of friendship, all that crap.

186
00:20:55.855 --> 00:20:58.589
You know the truth.
They're laughing at us.

187
00:20:58.591 --> 00:21:00.458
They think
their chess dominance...

188
00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:04.795
Proves Soviet intellectual
superiority over the decadent west.

189
00:21:04.797 --> 00:21:06.631
I don't really care
about politics.

190
00:21:06.633 --> 00:21:10.134
They're using chess to say "screw
America." I'm about the game, you see.

191
00:21:10.136 --> 00:21:12.136
Two guys at a board,
one makes a move,

192
00:21:12.138 --> 00:21:14.372
the other makes a move,
and that's it.

193
00:21:15.641 --> 00:21:17.608
I'm a chess fan myself.

194
00:21:20.579 --> 00:21:22.880
I'm also hopelessly patriotic.

195
00:21:25.717 --> 00:21:28.077
I take an interest in people
like yourself, creative people.

196
00:21:29.755 --> 00:21:33.457
I create the wherewithal that
allows them to do what they do.

197
00:21:33.459 --> 00:21:36.560
Ask Jimi Hendrix.
Ask the rolling stones.

198
00:21:36.562 --> 00:21:38.562
If I can help them,
I can help anybody.

199
00:21:38.564 --> 00:21:42.233
I'd like to represent
you, Mr. Fischer.

200
00:21:42.235 --> 00:21:44.268
So you're out to make a buck.

201
00:21:44.270 --> 00:21:46.404
No, I don't need the money.
I'd be doing this for free.

202
00:21:46.406 --> 00:21:48.572
Pro bono.

203
00:21:48.574 --> 00:21:51.809
You're the one man in this country
who could put up a fight.

204
00:21:51.811 --> 00:21:53.744
Maybe even beat them.

205
00:21:53.746 --> 00:21:56.180
I'd like a front-row seat
when the good guys win.

206
00:21:58.016 --> 00:22:01.185
If I went back to competition, there'd
have to be some real changes.

207
00:22:01.187 --> 00:22:02.820
It's got to be fair.

208
00:22:02.822 --> 00:22:05.456
If you're serious
about playing,

209
00:22:05.458 --> 00:22:07.358
I'll see what I can do.

210
00:22:08.593 --> 00:22:10.761
That is if you
still wanna play.

211
00:22:12.798 --> 00:22:14.265
Call me.

212
00:22:31.650 --> 00:22:33.718
He's very excited about this.

213
00:22:33.720 --> 00:22:35.353
I'm only a selector
on the committee.

214
00:22:35.355 --> 00:22:38.456
You see, he apologizes
to the federation.

215
00:22:38.458 --> 00:22:41.025
With profanity
on the first line.

216
00:22:41.027 --> 00:22:44.328
Ah. Well, he's...
he's nursed a grudge.

217
00:22:44.330 --> 00:22:45.896
Mm-hmm. For a long time.

218
00:22:45.898 --> 00:22:49.033
He's studied
how the Russians play.

219
00:22:49.035 --> 00:22:51.168
Every day.
Eighteen hours a day.

220
00:22:51.170 --> 00:22:52.970
For four years. Mm-hmm.

221
00:22:52.972 --> 00:22:57.508
For him, uh, Vietnam and the
Beatles never happened.

222
00:22:57.510 --> 00:23:00.845
I'm guessing he still has his
opinions about the Soviets?

223
00:23:00.847 --> 00:23:04.315
Well, you'll promise the committee,
we'll keep him out of trouble.

224
00:23:04.317 --> 00:23:07.385
The Piatigorsky was organized to
build Bridges, not to burn them.

225
00:23:08.887 --> 00:23:12.390
Well, so we lose 12-0,
and that's a bridge?

226
00:23:13.825 --> 00:23:16.260
He asked for you.

227
00:23:16.262 --> 00:23:17.628
Wants you to be his second.

228
00:23:19.865 --> 00:23:21.832
He respects you.

229
00:23:21.834 --> 00:23:23.567
You're the only one
who ever beat Spassky.

230
00:23:23.569 --> 00:23:26.003
We were young.
He'd destroy me now.

231
00:23:28.740 --> 00:23:31.542
And... You've beaten Bobby.

232
00:23:31.544 --> 00:23:33.444
That was a long time ago.

233
00:23:36.181 --> 00:23:37.748
Bobby has problems.

234
00:23:38.950 --> 00:23:40.484
So did Mozart.

235
00:23:43.889 --> 00:23:45.589
He might crack.

236
00:23:46.925 --> 00:23:49.293
Bobby won't crack.

237
00:23:50.195 --> 00:23:52.096
He will explode.

238
00:23:56.436 --> 00:23:59.370
Bobby? Bill's here. Oh.

239
00:23:59.372 --> 00:24:01.238
Hey, Bobby, how you doing?

240
00:24:01.240 --> 00:24:03.774
Against Petrosian in Zurich, you
sacrificed your king's pawn.

241
00:24:03.776 --> 00:24:05.776
You know that's the thing
that got you, right?

242
00:24:05.778 --> 00:24:08.646
You always play too cautiously and
